From 069bc2ee75728cd02ae7d80c6661dbd0dabcbed7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:57:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make template copies per item with screen params (issue 1)

registerScreens(["product_1", "product_2"], "item_settings") made copies
that produced identical instructions, so nothing item specific reached
the output.

- ScreenSpec gains `params`; they are stored on the Screen and resolved
  when instructions are built for every edge touching the screen, so
  template edges are written once with $NAME$ references.
- ITEM_ID defaults to the id after the template prefix when declared.
- Precedence: graph defaults < screen params < route variables < runtime.
- Params must be declared variables of the right type (UNKNOWN_PARAM,
  PARAM_TYPE); a bad one rejects the whole call.
- cloneTree copies params. Tests, README, llms.txt, AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG.
